"""Build the self-contained offline research page; standard library only."""
from pathlib import Path
from html import escape

HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent

def math(tex,display=False):
    return f'<span class="math{" display" if display else ""}" data-tex="{escape(tex,quote=True)}">{escape(tex)}</span>'

def links(folder,items):
    return '<div class="links">'+''.join(f'<a href="{folder}/{name}">{label} ↓</a>' for name,label in items)+'</div>'

def main():
    prooflinks=[('proof.tex','Complete LaTeX proof'),('certificate.json','Exact certificate'),
        ('verify_independently.py','Portable independent verifier'),('independent-verification.json','Exact verification report')]
    alpha=r'\alpha=\frac{\sqrt{1131}}{128},\qquad\beta=\frac{581\sqrt{1131}}{928}+i\frac{3289\sqrt{3045}}{4640}'
    coefficients=r'\begin{aligned}c_0=c_{24}&=\alpha,\\c_4=c_{20}&=\frac{42\alpha+\beta}{\sqrt{10626}},\\c_8=c_{16}&=\frac{591\alpha-4\beta}{\sqrt{735471}},\\c_{12}&=\frac{2828\alpha+6\beta}{\sqrt{2704156}}.\end{aligned}'
    text='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>24 and 26 qubits · Proven maximum AC orders</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../styles.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js" defer></script><style>main{max-width:1050px;padding-block:40px}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,48px)}h2{margin-top:40px}.display{display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:12px 0}.links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px 20px;margin-block:20px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}th,td{text-align:left;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.claim{padding:18px 22px;background:var(--paper-alt,#f0efe9);border-left:3px solid var(--accent,#5e4b7c)}pre{overflow-x:auto;padding:14px;background:var(--paper-alt,#f0efe9)}section{scroll-margin-top:24px}</style></head><body><main><a href="../../index.html">← Pure AC-state catalogue</a><p class="eyebrow">Exact states · Universal exclusions</p><h1>Twenty-four and twenty-six qubits</h1><p class="claim">The maximum pure AC order is seven at N=24 and six at N=26. The 24-qubit witness has explicit radical Dicke coefficients. The 26-qubit witness is an exact algebraic state defined by a certified polynomial root.</p>'''
    text+='<table><thead><tr><th>Qubits</th><th>Exact attained order</th><th>Maximum pure order</th><th>Construction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>24</th><td>7</td><td>'+math(r't_{\max}(24)=7')+'</td><td>Seven Dicke components; explicit radicals</td></tr><tr><th>26</th><td>6</td><td>'+math(r't_{\max}(26)=6')+'</td><td>Certified unique algebraic root</td></tr><tr><th>21</th><td>4</td><td>'+math(r'4\le t_{\max}(21)\le5')+'</td><td>Fifth-order existence remains open</td></tr></tbody></table>'
    text+='<section id="n24"><h2>24 qubits: explicit maximum-order state</h2><p>Use normalized Dicke states and set</p>'+math(alpha,True)
    text+='<p>The only nonzero coefficients of '+math(r'|\psi_{24}\rangle=\sum_{r=0}^{24}c_r|D_{24}^{(r)}\rangle')+' are</p>'+math(coefficients,True)
    text+='<p>They are generated compactly by two octahedral binary forms:</p>'+math(r'\sum_r\sqrt{\binom{24}{r}}c_rz^r=\alpha(1+14z^4+z^8)^3+\beta z^4(1-z^4)^4.',True)
    text+='<p>Exact Schmidt reductions and an independent direct partial trace verify normalization and</p>'+math(r'\rho_7=I_8/8,\qquad(\rho_8)_{00}-1/9=\frac{13}{155040}\ne0.',True)
    text+='<p>Thus this state is exactly seventh-order AC. Its 24 Majorana stars are distinct, verified by an exact polynomial gcd. The state has proper octahedral symmetry.</p><h3>Why order eight is impossible</h3><p>Choose the 24 Hilbert–Schmidt orthonormal tensor maps of ranks one through four from spin 12 to spin 11. Their pairwise products contain ranks at most eight. An eighth-order AC state would therefore map to 24 nonzero mutually orthogonal vectors in the spin-11 space, which has dimension 23. This contradiction applies to every complex symmetric state.</p>'+math(r'\langle T_a\psi,T_b\psi\rangle=\frac{\operatorname{Tr}(T_a^\dagger T_b)}{25}=\frac{\delta_{ab}}{25},\qquad24>23.',True)
    text+='<p><a href="../../index.html#n=24&amp;t=7&amp;state=octahedral-n24-t7">Open the exact state and its Majorana sphere ↗</a></p>'
    text+=links('n24-t7',[('proof.tex','Analytical construction and upper-bound proof'),('states.json','Exact radical Dicke components'),('build_witness.py','Portable construction'),('verify_witness.py','Independent direct-trace verifier'),('independent-verification.json','Exact verification report')])+'</section>'

    text+='<section id="n26"><h2>26 qubits: a certified exact algebraic state</h2><p>The refined Liège state supplies a numerical starting point. A rational contraction certificate proves that an exact state exists nearby. Its definition is</p>'+math(r'|\psi_{26}\rangle=\sum_{r=0}^{26}\frac{\sqrt{\binom{26}{r}}}{d_r}(x_r^*+ix_{27+r}^*)|D_{26}^{(r)}\rangle.',True)
    text+='<p>The certificate records the integer scales '+math(r'd_r')+', a rational center '+math(r'x^0\in\mathbb Q^{54}')+', five fixed coordinates, and the order of 49 active coordinates. The exact values '+math(r'x^*')+' are the unique real root in the specified box of the 49 rational quadratic equations equivalent to '+math(r'\rho_6=I_7/7')+'. No closed-form radical components are claimed.</p>'
    text+='<h3>Existence from an exact contraction</h3><p>After fixing the five rational coordinates, define '+math(r'T(y)=y-AF(y)')+' using the saved rational matrix '+math(r'A')+'. An independent standard-library verifier reconstructs the equations and the exact Jacobian, then proves</p>'+math(r'\begin{gathered}r=10^{-65},\quad\|AF(y^0)\|_\infty<10^{-67},\\\|I-ADF(y^0)\|_\infty<10^{-76},\quad\|A\|_\infty<17000,\\H\le2^{22},\qquad q\le\|I-ADF(y^0)\|_\infty+\|A\|_\infty Hr<10^{-54}.\end{gathered}',True)
    text+='<p>The exact bounds show that '+math(r'T')+' is a contraction and maps the radius-'+math(r'r')+' box strictly into itself. Banach’s theorem gives a unique fixed point. The inverse-defect bound makes '+math(r'A')+' invertible, so this point solves '+math(r'F=0')+'. Its nonsingular rational polynomial equations make its coordinates algebraic. The identity reduction also proves exact normalization.</p>'
    text+='<p>Each real or imaginary Dicke component is within '+math(r'2\cdot10^{-65}')+' of the exact rational-center conversion. The saved decimal components and copied nearby Majorana coordinates are numerical renderings; the equations and isolating box define the exact state.</p>'
    text+='<h3>Why order seven is impossible</h3><p>An exact three-copy positivity certificate excludes every seventh-order pure symmetric state at N=26. The proof uses necessary low-multipole contractions and positive partial time reversal of a rotationally averaged tensor-power projector. A rational separating identity gives a contradiction for every hypothetical state. An independent verifier reconstructs the representation, contractions, partial-transpose embedding and positive-matrix factorizations. This upper bound and the certified sixth-order state prove the maximum six.</p>'
    text+='<p><a href="../../index.html#n=26&amp;t=6&amp;state=certified-algebraic-n26-t6">Open the certified state and its Majorana sphere ↗</a></p>'
    text+=links('n26-t6',prooflinks)
    text+='<h3>Seventh-order exclusion</h3>'+links('n26-t7',prooflinks+[('positive_control.py','Independent complex-state embedding control'),('positive-control.json','Exact control report')])
    text+='<details><summary>Additional eighth-order certificate</summary><p>This weaker auxiliary upper bound is retained for reproducibility. The seventh-order exclusion above is the one needed to prove maximum order six.</p>'+links('n26-t8',prooflinks)+'</details></section>'

    text+='<section id="n21"><h2>21 qubits: what remains open</h2><p>The exact fourth-order state and universal sixth-order exclusion establish '+math(r'4\le t_{\max}(21)\le5')+'. The remaining question is whether a fifth-order pure state exists. A failed numerical search or a feasible moment relaxation does not settle that question. The catalogue keeps it unresolved.</p><p><a href="../n21-n22/index.html#n21">Read the exact 21-qubit construction and rigorous bounds ↗</a></p></section>'
    text+='<section id="reproduce"><h2>Reproduce the proofs offline</h2><p>The N24 construction and direct-trace verifier require SymPy. The N26 contraction and exclusion verifiers require only Python’s standard library and read the certificates beside them.</p><pre><code>python3 n24-t7/build_witness.py\npython3 n24-t7/verify_witness.py\npython3 n26-t6/verify_independently.py\npython3 n26-t7/verify_independently.py\npython3 n26-t7/positive_control.py\npython3 n26-t8/verify_independently.py</code></pre><p>The optional <a href="n26-t6/build.py">N26 discovery script</a> accepts a source catalogue through <code>--source</code>; numerical discovery is separate from the portable proof.</p><div class="links"><a href="states.json">Combined state records ↓</a><a href="build_states.py">Rebuild the combined records ↓</a><a href="build_page.py">Rebuild this page ↓</a></div></section>'
    text+='</main><script>document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",()=>{for(const el of document.querySelectorAll("[data-tex]"))katex.render(el.dataset.tex,el,{displayMode:el.classList.contains("display"),throwOnError:true});});</script></body></html>'
    (HERE/'index.html').write_text(text)
    print('Built offline research page for exact maxima at N24 and N26.')

if __name__=='__main__':main()
